formation and mcreases m an ascendmg one, the amphtude'P changes m the same dIrectIOn as the modulus ma Gauss transformatIOn but in the OppOSIte directlOn ma Landen transformatlOn. Accordmg to thIS termmology, WhICh IS not universal, the ascendmg and descendmg Landen transformatlOns have been put m algebraIC form by DIDonato and Hershey [3] for computatIOn of F and E The algorIthm for the descendmg case IS mcomplete m the absence of a rule to determme the correct branch of an inverse CIrcular functlOn at the end of the calculatlOn. A mamly algebraIC version of the ascendmg Gauss transformatlOn has been gIVen by Carlson [4], but only for the mtegral of the first kmd, a consider-},
	author = {Carlson, Bille C},
	journal = {Journal of Mathematics and Physics},
